BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Configuration & Vulnerability Management Policy) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 697.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 674.0 Td (This policy establishes Hewlett Packard Enterprise's \(HPE\) requirements for securely configuring,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660.0 Td (maintaining, and continuously assessing all information systems, endpoints, network devices,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646.0 Td (container images, and cloud workloads across the enterprise. It applies to every asset owned,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632.0 Td (operated, or managed by HPE, including on-premises data centers, hybrid environments, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (third-party cloud platforms. The objective is to ensure that systems are provisioned from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 604.0 Td (known-secure state, kept current against emerging threats, and continuously validated against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590.0 Td (recognized industry standards.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 564.0 Td (2. Secure Baseline and Hardening Configurations) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541.0 Td (Every system class deployed at HPE must be built from an approved standard build derived from a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527.0 Td (documented golden image. These baseline configurations define the authoritative hardened state for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 513.0 Td (operating systems, middleware, databases, and container base images. Hardening requirements are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 499.0 Td (aligned to CIS Benchmarks as the primary reference. Where systems support regulated or government) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 485.0 Td (workloads, the applicable DISA STIG guidance is layered on top of the CIS baseline to satisfy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 471.0 Td (stricter federal requirements. Additional industry standards, including NIST SP 800-53 and vendor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 457.0 Td (security guides, are incorporated where they address gaps not covered by CIS or STIG.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437.0 Td (Golden images are version-controlled, cryptographically signed, and stored in a centrally governed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 423.0 Td (artifact repository. Baselines are reviewed at least annually and whenever a benchmark revision,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 409.0 Td (major OS release, or significant threat change occurs. Manual, one-off system builds outside the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 395.0 Td (approved baseline are prohibited.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 369.0 Td (3. Infrastructure-as-Code and Automation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346.0 Td (HPE provisions and configures infrastructure primarily through infrastructure-as-code \(IaC\). All) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332.0 Td (hardening controls, package versions, and security settings are codified in declarative templates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318.0 Td (\(Terraform, Ansible, and Kubernetes manifests\) and delivered through automated CI/CD pipelines. This) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 304.0 Td (orchestration-driven approach guarantees that the hardened baseline is applied consistently and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290.0 Td (repeatably at every deployment, eliminating human error inherent in manual configuration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 270.0 Td (Security controls are embedded directly into the pipeline: IaC templates are statically scanned for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 256.0 Td (misconfigurations before merge, and no build may promote to production without passing automated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 242.0 Td (policy gates. Automation enforces that the running state of an asset always matches its codified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 228.0 Td (definition, and pipelines re-apply the golden configuration on every release to prevent silent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214.0 Td (divergence.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 188.0 Td (4. Patch and Vulnerability Management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 165.0 Td (HPE maintains a continuous patch management program covering operating systems, applications,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151.0 Td (firmware, and container images. Security updates, hotfixes, and vendor patches are evaluated against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 137.0 Td (risk and deployed according to defined service levels based on severity:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 117.0 Td (- Critical vulnerabilities: remediated within 7 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 103.0 Td (- High: remediated within 30 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 89.0 Td (- Medium: remediated within 90 days) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75.0 Td (- Low: remediated during the next scheduled maintenance cycle) Tj ET
