BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (Newly identified vulnerabilities are triaged using CVSS scores enriched with threat intelligence and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (exploitability data. Wherever feasible, remediation is delivered by rebuilding from an updated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (golden image and redeploying through the pipeline rather than patching live systems in place,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (ensuring the fix is durable and reflected in the baseline.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 670.0 Td (5. Compliance Scanning and Assessment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 647.0 Td (Automated compliance scanning runs continuously across the estate. Authenticated configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 633.0 Td (checks measure each asset against its assigned CIS Benchmark and STIG baseline, while vulnerability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619.0 Td (scanners perform recurring assessment of exposed weaknesses. Scan results feed a centralized) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 605.0 Td (dashboard that reports posture by business unit and asset class. Internal and independent audits are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 591.0 Td (conducted periodically to validate that scanning coverage, controls, and remediation timelines meet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577.0 Td (policy and regulatory obligations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 551.0 Td (6. Configuration Drift and Deviation Handling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528.0 Td (Any deviation from the approved baseline is treated as a security event. Continuous monitoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 514.0 Td (detects configuration drift by comparing the live state of assets to their codified IaC definitions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 500.0 Td (and hardened baselines. When unauthorized variance is identified, automated remediation restores the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 486.0 Td (system to its known-good state, or the drift is escalated to the system owner for investigation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 466.0 Td (Legitimate business needs that require departing from a baseline must be documented through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 452.0 Td (formal exceptions and waivers process. Each requested exception must include a business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 438.0 Td (justification, risk assessment, compensating controls, and an approved expiration date. Waivers are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 424.0 Td (reviewed and reauthorized at defined intervals by the Security Governance team; expired exceptions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 410.0 Td (are automatically flagged as non-compliant.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 384.0 Td (7. Roles and Enforcement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 361.0 Td (The Information Security organization owns this policy, maintains the baseline library, and operates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 347.0 Td (scanning and reporting tooling. System and application owners are accountable for remediating) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333.0 Td (findings and keeping their assets compliant. Violations of this policy may result in system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319.0 Td (isolation, revocation of deployment privileges, and disciplinary action.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 293.0 Td (8. Review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 270.0 Td (This policy is reviewed at least annually and updated in response to changes in CIS Benchmarks, STIG) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 256.0 Td (releases, regulatory requirements, or the HPE threat landscape.) Tj ET
